  "reason": "RNA-only PCA single-profile is much stronger than image-only ResNet (0.485 vs 0.208 accuracy; 0.464 vs 0.172 F1), so RNA is the more promising direction. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the RNA signal. config_002 tests this by keeping the same PCA RNA encoder and adding multiprofile avgpool, isolating the profile/aggregation effect with minimal added complexity. This is a logical exploitation of the strongest result and will clarify whether more complex transformer or multimodal extensions are worth testing."
